window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-ibuki-mio"]=[{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ch 2  2 6 2 8  the class c girl with the swollen cheek a path in the forest on the way back to camp  she sits against a large tree  not a class d student  with a red  swollen mark on her cheek","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.6–§2.8: the Class C girl with the swollen cheek<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.78–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A path in the forest on the way back to camp; she sits against a large tree, not a Class D student, with a red, swollen mark on her cheek.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;Just a class dispute. Don’t worry about it&quot; — her answer when asked who did it; &quot;her voice was low and even, but it was clear she wasn’t feeling well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Names the barrier herself: “I’m from Class C. In other words, I’m your enemy. You understand that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Refuses the base-camp offer — &quot;There’s no way I could do something like that&quot; — then watches them refuse to leave: &quot;You guys are really stupid. You’re not acting logically. You aren’t thinking about your own class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Introductions after the standoff: “I’m…Ibuki” — and she won&#x27;t meet his eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Dirt under her nails and disturbed soil where she sat — the page shows the fight without naming who won it.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The account, once Hirata&#x27;s offer sticks: &quot;I had a fight with a boy in my class. He hit me and chased me away. That’s all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> On his decency: “He’s seriously a good-natured guy, isn’t he?” — and the Class C verdict: &quot;Not at all… There isn’t really anyone in Class C like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Gets Kushida&#x27;s group ration — &quot;Are you guys stupid? You’re all being way too nice.&quot; — and is told to eat first, talk later.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Told to wait while the class decides; the class agrees to shelter her once roll-call attrition makes it profitable, not only decent.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  the camera in her bag the luggage pile outside the tent before dawn  her singularly colored bag is easy to spot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The luggage pile outside the tent before dawn; her singularly colored bag is easy to spot.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Her rented digital camera — no data, no sign it was ever used — is found in the bag while she sleeps and put back untouched.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.6–§2.8: the Class C girl with the swollen cheek<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 1  the visit to the campsite class c s boys stride into the campsite  a pained expression flashes across her face and she ducks behind the tent to hide   do you know ryuuen   i don t think they were looking for me   i wonder if things are heading toward that worst case scenario i imagined","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class C&#x27;s boys stride into the campsite; a pained expression flashes across her face and she ducks behind the tent to hide.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you know Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don&#x27;t think they were looking for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wonder if things are heading toward that worst-case scenario I imagined…”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sounds irritated discussing him — “as if she were discussing a family enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Komiya and Kondou are his underlings; his name alone puts her behind the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the new suspect<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ch 6  6 1  the new suspect sitting at the far edge of the camp  she becomes the class s new prey the moment someone says her name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the new suspect<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sitting at the far edge of the camp, she becomes the class’s new prey the moment someone says her name.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The collective’s doubts swing to her instantly; she is the outsider from Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Hey. What if it was that girl, Ibuki?” and the sabotage theory that follows are left untagged in the translation.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p181-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2: the test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p181-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ch 6  6 2  the test walks up to ayanokoji alone after the morning s accusations and tests whether he suspects her   do you have a minute   what you were talking about this morning sounded really serious  the   underwear incident  i mean  i mean  class d isn t a monolith   whatever the reason  stealing a girl s underwear is unforgivable   do you doubt me  by any chance   are you the culprit   okay  that s good  well  it s not like i had any evidence or anything  it looks like some of the girls trust you and that boy hirata  i think the chance of you being a villain is low   do you have any idea who the culprit is   so who do you think did it   if a boy isn t the culprit  then they ll suspect me the stranger next  i m absolutely certain some people have already said something about me  after all  i could ve just made it look like the guys stole the underwear  right   thank you  i didn t think you would say something like that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p181-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2: the test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.181–183<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks up to Ayanokōji alone after the morning’s accusations and tests whether he suspects her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What you were talking about this morning sounded really serious. The … underwear incident, I mean. I mean, Class D isn’t a monolith.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Whatever the reason, stealing a girl’s underwear is unforgivable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Yamauchi had taken her in, and Kushida’s group was looking after her — no particular reason to seek him out.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you doubt me, by any chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you the culprit?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, that’s good. Well, it’s not like I had any evidence or anything. It looks like some of the girls trust you and that boy Hirata. I think the chance of you being a villain is low.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you have any idea who the culprit is?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So who do you think did it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Asks as if she were testing him, glancing at him out of the corner of her eye.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If a boy isn’t the culprit, then they’ll suspect me—the stranger—next. I’m absolutely certain some people have already said something about me. After all, I could’ve just made it look like the guys stole the underwear. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. I didn’t think you would say something like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He says he trusts her while his own narration names her the culprit.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the new suspect<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p194-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.4: joining the search<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p194-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ch 6  6 4  joining the search invited along on the last forage  she agrees out of a debt to class d   okay  i owe class d a debt of gratitude  sure  i ll help","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.4: joining the search<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.194–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Invited along on the last forage, she agrees out of a debt to Class D.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Okay. I owe Class D a debt of gratitude… Sure, I’ll help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Slings her bag over her shoulder and steps into the forest with the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Paired with Kushida for the search — the last two left once the others split.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p181-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2: the test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p201-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.5: the shower line<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p201-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ibuki-mio","q":"ch 6  6 5  the shower line waits out the river swim in the shower queue   the line position that will later clear karuizawa  and place her   i ll pass  i don t really like swimming  so i ll just wait to use the shower room   whoa  looks like it s moving now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p201-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.5: the shower line<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.201–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits out the river swim in the shower queue — the line position that will later clear Karuizawa, and place her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll pass. I don’t really like swimming, so I’ll just wait to use the shower room,”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Whoa, looks like it’s moving now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the tail of the line behind Karuizawa’s group and Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Sakura follows her lead in refusing the swim; the two wait in line together.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p194-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.4: joining the search<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p206-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.7: the fire she did not set<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p206-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ch 6  6 7  the fire she did not set stands at the burning bundle wearing such genuine confusion that horikita hesitates to call her over","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.7: the fire she did not set<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.206–208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands at the burning bundle wearing such genuine confusion that Horikita hesitates to call her over.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Slips away with one of the bags while suspicion turns on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Held as the likeliest culprit by Horikita — and watched being surprised by a fire she insists later she did not start.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p201-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.5: the shower line<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.8: cornered in the rain<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p213-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ch 6  6 8  cornered in the rain waits in the mud knowing horikita is behind her  then turns and talks her in circles until the fight starts   what are you doing  horikita   when did you notice me   right from the start   why were you following me   do you really not know   no  i don t know   you clearly know why i was following you  don t you   i really have no idea what you re talking about   why should i lie   i d at least like to hear why you followed me  from your own lips   the underwear theft and the fire  misfortune continues to befall class d   so what   do you realize that some people suspect you   ah  i suppose since i m an outsider  there s not much i can do about that   that s what i m talking about   you re saying i m the culprit  do you have any proof   unfortunately  i don t have a single shred of evidence related to the underwear theft  but i think it was you   that s a pretty terrible thing to say  you don t have any evidence  yet you suspect me   i suspect you because of today  you don t need me to explain that  do you   let me cut to the chase  i want you to return something you took from me   i don t know what you re talking about   where are you going   who knows   how long are you going to follow me  don t you think enough is enough   once you return what you stole from me   why don t you calm down and try thinking  if i stole the keycard  would i have held onto it  if someone saw me with it  that would mean immediate disqualification  i d only end up lo","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.8: cornered in the rain<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.213–220<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits in the mud knowing Horikita is behind her, then turns and talks her in circles until the fight starts.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you doing, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “When did you notice me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Right from the start.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>56 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why were you following me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you really not know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I don’t know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You clearly know why I was following you, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really have no idea what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why should I lie?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d at least like to hear why you followed me, from your own lips.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The underwear theft and the fire. Misfortune continues to befall Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you realize that some people suspect you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. I suppose since I’m an outsider, there’s not much I can do about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what I’m talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re saying I’m the culprit? Do you have any proof?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, I don’t have a single shred of evidence related to the underwear theft. But I think it was you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a pretty terrible thing to say. You don’t have any evidence, yet you suspect me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> As Horikita assesses her: laid low since day five, kept her distance from Class D, and — contrary to expectations — was not suspected.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suspect you because of today. You don’t need me to explain that, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me cut to the chase. I want you to return something you took from me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Where are you going?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How long are you going to follow me? Don’t you think enough is enough?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Once you return what you stole from me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why don’t you calm down and try thinking? If I stole the keycard, would I have held onto it? If someone saw me with it, that would mean immediate disqualification. I’d only end up losing points myself, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Lets the word “keycard” slip when Horikita never said it — the confession by mistake the narration catches for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You thought I confessed to something, didn’t you? You’re wrong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m tired of talking with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Digs in the ground with both hands while Horikita falters against a tree.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your condition has gotten a lot worse, hasn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ibuki-san. I’m going to investigate you with everything I’ve got. You don’t mind?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With everything you’ve got? Could you be a bit more specific? You mean you’re going to resort to violence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My last warning, huh? Oh, I get it. I get it. Why don’t you get your wish?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Drops the bag and raises her arms as if surrendering — and kicks the moment Horikita reaches for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, you’re good,”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone might see us here, you mean? Weren’t you willing to use violence, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs Horikita’s shoulders and throws her into the mud, sneering from above.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you like a moment to rest?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? You can really move, surprisingly. You practice or something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Sizes Horikita’s martial arts up without panic and enjoys the exchange — white teeth showing the whole while.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve been trying really hard until now. I’ll tell you the truth, as a reward. I stole the card.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Draws the card out of her pocket and shows the engraved name.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You gave up the truth pretty easily.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t matter if I admit it or not now. There’s no evidence I used violence against you. It’s not as though the school can make a judgment here. Isn’t that right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Involved? In what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t burn the manual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The denial comes out after a hesitation — she stole the card but insists the fire was not hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You intend to keep lying even now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What would I gain by burning it? It was inevitable that people would begin searching for the criminal after the uproar. Besides, people would suspect me rather strongly. There was nothing to gain and a lot to lose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t understand… I thought you were involved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think he’s in Class D? There’s a guy who figured me out before you did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She leaves the man unnamed; the page names no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So. You can’t mean…”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This conversation is over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ends the talk with a blow to the head, sweeps her leg, slaps her cheek, and kicks her in the face on the last try to rise.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think they’ll permit such coercive methods?”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, now. I don’t feel like answering that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p206-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.7: the fire she did not set<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p221-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.9: the handover<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p221-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ch 6  6 9  the handover her viewpoint  she stands over the unconscious horikita  digs up the flashlight and transceiver  and calls her leader in   what   is it because of the rain   yo  excellent work  ibuki  you did well   naturally  yes   naturally  if you hadn t made any mistakes until now  i wouldn t have had to risk coming over here   that couldn t be helped  i hadn t planned for the digital camera to break   so  where s the card   it s here   you come over here and confirm it  too  that was your condition  remember  relax  it s dark out  and this weather is horrible  there shouldn t be anyone here  it s great to be cautious  but don t waste time   it looks like the real thing   you managed to infiltrate class d quite well  weren t you suspected   under normal circumstances  i would have been  but as for my methods  that s a trade secret   don t sit there and think about it forever  the situation is black and white  so make your decision  you re already halfway there  don t do something as stupid as pulling out here   you re right   if this wasn t an honorable deed  then what are you going to do  did you know that sakayanagi s faction has dominated ever since rumors spread that you failed to get on the student council despite your best efforts  this might be your chance  right   you bastard  why are you telling me this   class a maintains its position by forming alliances  if you can form those  even those who have double crossed you will return under your wing  won t th","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.9: the handover<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.221–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her viewpoint: she stands over the unconscious Horikita, digs up the flashlight and transceiver, and calls her leader in.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What?”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is it because of the rain?”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Yo. Excellent work, Ibuki. You did well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>40 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The buried items seem slightly different from when she hid them — her own doubt, unresolved on the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reports her location over the transceiver and waits half an hour for his blinking flashlight.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Naturally, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Naturally? If you hadn’t made any mistakes until now, I wouldn’t have had to risk coming over here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That couldn’t be helped. I hadn’t planned for the digital camera to break.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The camera’s breaking forced her to carry the card instead of photographing it — the risk that let Horikita catch her.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, where’s the card?”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands the card over; Ryuuen checks the engraved name under his flashlight.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Watches him come out of the shadows to inspect the card under the condition he set.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You come over here and confirm it, too. That was your condition, remember? Relax, it’s dark out, and this weather is horrible. There shouldn’t be anyone here. It’s great to be cautious, but don’t waste time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It looks like the real thing,”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You managed to infiltrate Class D quite well. Weren’t you suspected?”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question carries no speaker tag; it follows his inspection of the card and her methods, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Under normal circumstances, I would have been. But as for my methods, that’s a trade secret.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The spying operation from the test’s start: Ryuuen slapped her to make the lie true, and Class D read her as beaten and chased out of her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t sit there and think about it forever. The situation is black-and-white, so make your decision. You’re already halfway there. Don’t do something as stupid as pulling out here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The assent is untagged; it sits under Ryuuen’s pressure, and the narration still reads him as not having consented.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If this wasn’t an honorable deed, then what are you going to do? Did you know that Sakayanagi’s faction has dominated ever since rumors spread that you failed to get on the student council despite your best efforts? This might be your chance, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You bastard. Why are you telling me this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class A maintains its position by forming alliances. If you can form those, even those who have double-crossed you will return under your wing, won’t they? Or you could make me your enemy, I suppose? If you do, I wonder what would happen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sakayanagi is absent. It’s impossible for someone indecisive to rule Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ve established negotiations, as promised. I accept your proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s good. You’ve exercised sound judgment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, what negotiation? Would you explain?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To form an alliance. With Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll be heading back now. I don’t want to risk things by lingering for too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Watches Katsuragi return the card and disappear into the darkness.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about the negotiation? What was discussed? What are we getting in return?”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But…is there any guarantee Katsuragi will keep his promise? He might renege.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The doubt and the answer that follows both run untagged; the answer is recorded as Ryuuen’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have that covered, of course. He will have no choice but to honor his promise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lays out the contract’s terms to her with a creepy smile — the page never quotes them.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Everything was going according to Ryuuen’s plan, including the fact that most of our students had retired.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “he was probably the man with abilities closest to those of Class A, after all. I had to acknowledge it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Wipes her fingerprints from the card and sticks it back in Horikita’s hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reads her as no threat — untrusting, unreported, enduring in silence — and leaves the card with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Use your smarts to protect yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Says it to the unconscious Horikita, then disappears with Ryuuen into the dark woods.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.8: cornered in the rain<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p241-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the culprit named<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p241-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ch 7  the culprit named named everywhere she is absent   the emptied beach  karuizawa s apology  and the lounge retelling that finally explains how her theft fit a larger plan   ibuki san stole my underwear  ayanokouji kun told us everything   horikita san  when you noticed that ibuki san was the culprit  she tried to run because you questioned her  right  that s why you ended up collapsing and getting sick   but wait  ibuki san stole my card  but what if i d protected it really thoroughly   did you drop the card on purpose back then  well  i suppose that yamauchi kun s actions might have provided ibuki san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the culprit named<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.241–256<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named everywhere she is absent — the emptied beach, Karuizawa’s apology, and the lounge retelling that finally explains how her theft fit a larger plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ibuki-san stole my underwear. Ayanokouji-kun told us everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Horikita-san, when you noticed that Ibuki-san was the culprit, she tried to run because you questioned her, right? That’s why you ended up collapsing and getting sick…”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “But wait. Ibuki-san stole my card, but what if I’d protected it really thoroughly?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nowhere on the sandy beach when the Class C camp is found emptied, as if she’d retired as well.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The culprit Karuizawa names to her face; the chase and collapse of the sixth day are what the apology is about.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you drop the card on purpose back then? Well, I suppose that Yamauchi-kun’s actions might have provided Ibuki-san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki was picked up by Class D, but not by chance — the near-coincidence of two people saved by two separate classes dissolved once Kaneda in Class B came out as a spy Ryuuen had sent.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The bigger the lie, the more obvious the habit — she looked him straight in the eye even over the underwear theft.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The one who read her eye-contact habit and her camera plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki carried a digital camera to take a picture of the keycard; a photo would have made the leader’s identity clear to anyone and let her profit.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His spy on the island — the card, the camera and the transceiver all served the plan, and people outside Class C wanted her evidence rather than her word.<span class=\"pg\">p.255–256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact; Ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation — no one else controlled it, and his mistake was trusting no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p221-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.9: the handover<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ch 2  2 0  a passing mention as the culprit named once as the underwear culprit  ayanokoji asks whether karuizawa got hers back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the underwear culprit; Ayanokōji asks whether Karuizawa got hers back.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata confirms the fallout: naming her resolved things — “When she heard Ibuki-san was the culprit, things went smoothly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 0 3 1  the cafe shadow and the rabbit holdout walks into blue ocean at ryuen s side as the island spy horikita caught  later sits silent through the whole rabbit first discussion until ichinose calls her name   i m not so stupid that i d let someone like her see through me  things were simply more difficult because of my fever   on losing to horikita   in that case  let s have a rematch  she challenged   so what about sakayanagi  ibuki asked that  not horikita  she wanted to confirm that information herself  apparently   whatever  i don t really have anything to add  said ibuki","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.68–75, p.88<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into Blue Ocean at Ryūen’s side as the island spy Horikita caught; later sits silent through the whole Rabbit first discussion until Ichinose calls her name.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not so stupid that I’d let someone like her see through me. Things were simply more difficult because of my fever.” (on losing to Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In that case, let’s have a rematch,” she challenged.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So what about Sakayanagi?” Ibuki asked that, not Horikita. She wanted to confirm that information herself, apparently.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Closes the distance on Horikita ready to lunge, then stops — rules, and Ryūen’s leash, hold her back; “Tch!”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Clearly detests working beneath Ryūen, yet is exceptionally talented — the precise reason he chose her as the Class D spy.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The one question she puts to Ryūen all morning; he goes silent before answering.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sits “a little further away, as if isolating themselves” in the Rabbit circle — same posture as Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ayanokōji expected a fight with Karuizawa over the stolen underwear; Ibuki shows no tiredness and no revenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever. I don’t really have anything to add,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sole Class C holdout on the Katsuragi no-discussion vote — arms crossed since the test began, she does not move and does not speak until called; the others take it as her normal way.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His lackey on the reconnaissance walk; she detests the leash but keeps it.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The spy she failed against; rematch refused on rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl whose underwear she stole on the island — they share the Rabbit room without speaking.<span class=\"pg\">p.80, 88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Answers only when Ichinose asks her by name.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 1  the outsider s verdict watches the manabe karuizawa picture fight from the circle and speaks once  as an outsider   stupid  said ibuki   that s right  this absolutely has nothing to do with me  so i said what i thought as an outsider","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–95<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the Manabe–Karuizawa picture fight from the circle and speaks once, as an outsider.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Stupid,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s right. This absolutely has nothing to do with me. So I said what I thought as an outsider.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Crosses her arms and looks away; Manabe does not confront her — the narration reads a clear Class C hierarchy with Ibuki above Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Looks scornfully over at Manabe, showing her contempt, while the other Class C girls laugh at Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Above her in the Class C pecking order.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The only Class C voice that does not pile on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ch 4  4 0  not at the shade meeting named once as absent from ryuuen s side when he drops into the horikita conversation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.128<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as absent from Ryuuen’s side when he drops into the Horikita conversation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “He wasn’t with Ibuki, apparently” — the usual pair is split for this scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue and no further presence in the range.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the absent buffer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho ibuki-mio","q":"ch 4  4 2  the absent buffer named as the class c girl who might have mitigated the trio on karuizawa s tail   and she wasn t around","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2: the absent buffer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.159<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the Class C girl who might have mitigated the trio on Karuizawa’s tail — and she wasn’t around.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her absence is why the three can close on Karuizawa alone in the corridor.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The buffer between Manabe’s set and Karuizawa is missing for the stairwell.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue in this range; presence is the narrator’s counterfactual.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
